  "content": {
    "text": "13 hours ago\nNuvalent surges on GSK deal, and other early market movers.\nHere are some of the stocks making notable moves in Tuesday's premarket action:\nNuvalent shares are jumping nearly 40% after the U.S. biotech company agreed to be bought by the U.K.'s GSK in a $10.6 billion deal.\nShares of Vail Resorts are down about 4% after the ski-resorts operator said weather conditions remained unfavorable as it lowered its outlook.\nWolfspeed shares are up more than 6% after the semiconductor company agreed to collaborate with GE Aerospace on high-voltage silicon carbide power electronics.\nMicron Technology shares are following up Monday's 9.9% jump with a further 4% advance after memory stocks rebounded sharply in South Korea overnight.",
